IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa20-part27-merger`
IMPORT `coa-proc-merger`

-- coa-proc-merger-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-merger.l4 (Companies Act 2006, Part 27, Chapter 2, ss 902 to 918).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- The dates used throughout: the registrar receives the copy of the draft terms on 1 February 2026 and the first meeting is on 2 April 2026,
-- so the last day for the notice is 2 March 2026, 29 days after the receipt (February 2026 has 28 days); the period of one month before the meeting
-- begins on 2 March 2026 and ends on 2 April 2026, 31 days later (March has 31 days).

§ `Tests for the merger procedure`

§§ `Fixtures: dates`

`the receipt date` MEANS Date 1 2 2026
`the meeting date` MEANS Date 2 4 2026
`a receipt date too late for the notice` MEANS Date 10 3 2026
`a receipt date on the last day for the notice` MEANS Date 2 3 2026

§§ `Fixtures: the schemes (the eighteen fields, in order)`

-- the fields, in order: the company is public; a compromise or arrangement is proposed; it is for a reconstruction or amalgamation; the consideration is shares;
-- the company is being wound up; one or more public companies' undertaking is to be transferred; to another existing public company; two or more public companies'
-- undertaking is to be transferred; to a new company; all the relevant securities are held by the transferee; the percentages held; s 915A(3); s 915A(4);
-- s 918A(1); s 916(2); s 917(2); the arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A (a Boolean, from which s 917A(1) is called); s 918(1).
`scheme: absorption, nothing held` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: formation of a new company` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, (LIST 0), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, all securities held` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (LIST 100), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, all securities held, no meeting required` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (LIST 100), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 92), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, 92% held, second condition not met` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 92), (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, reports dispensed with by agreement` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, a Part 26A arrangement` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), TRUE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: not a public company` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: company being wound up` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)

§§ `Fixtures: the votes of one class (number present and voting, number for, value present and voting, value for)`

`votes: three of four in number and 80% in value` MEANS `s 907(1) votes of a class of members` OF 4, 3, 100, 80
`votes: two of four in number and 90% in value` MEANS `s 907(1) votes of a class of members` OF 4, 2, 100, 90
`votes: three of four in number and exactly 75% in value` MEANS `s 907(1) votes of a class of members` OF 4, 3, 100, 75
`votes: three of four in number and 74% in value` MEANS `s 907(1) votes of a class of members` OF 4, 3, 100, 74
`classes: one class that votes for` MEANS LIST `votes: three of four in number and 80% in value`
`classes: one class with exactly half in number` MEANS LIST `votes: two of four in number and 90% in value`
`classes: one class with exactly 75% in value` MEANS LIST `votes: three of four in number and exactly 75% in value`
`classes: one class with 74% in value` MEANS LIST `votes: three of four in number and 74% in value`

§§ `Assertions: the gates`

-- s 902(1), s 904(1)(a): a merger by absorption of public companies for shares, not in a winding up, is within the Part.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`
-- s 902(1), s 904(1)(b): a merger by formation of a new company is within the Part.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` `scheme: formation of a new company`
-- s 902(1)(a): the Part needs a public company.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` `scheme: not a public company`))
-- s 902(3): the Part does not apply where the company is being wound up.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` `scheme: company being wound up`))
-- s 904(1)(a): absorption is a merger by absorption; s 904(1)(b): formation of a new company is not.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` `scheme: formation of a new company`))
-- s 908(1): the report is required where nothing is held (nothing in ss 915 or 915A switches it off), and where the 92% holder's second condition is not met.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 section 908 requires the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 section 908 requires the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, second condition not met`
-- s 915(4): all the relevant securities held, so ss 908 and 909 do not apply.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 908 requires the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 909 requires the expert's report` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`))
-- s 915A(2): 90% or more but not all held, both conditions met, so ss 908, 909, 910 and 911 do not apply.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 908 requires the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 909 requires the expert's report` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 910 requires the supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 911 requires the documents to be open to inspection` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met`))
-- s 918A(1): agreement dispenses with the reports.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 908 requires the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, reports dispensed with by agreement`))
-- s 915 does not switch off s 910: a holder of all the securities still prepares the statement where s 910 applies.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 section 910 requires the supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`
-- s 911(7): inspection is switched off only by s 915A, so it stands where all the securities are held.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 section 911 requires the documents to be open to inspection` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`
-- s 907(1) and (2): a meeting is required unless one of ss 916 to 918 says it is not.
#ASSERT `ss 902-918 section 907 requires a meeting of the members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 907 requires a meeting of the members` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, no meeting required`))
-- s 917A(1): a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A needs no approval by the members of the company in respect of which it is proposed.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 902-918 section 907 requires a meeting of the members` `scheme: absorption, a Part 26A arrangement`))

§§ `Traces: s 905(1), the draft terms`

-- s 905(1): the directors draw up and adopt the draft terms on day 12; the text gives no time, so the day does not matter.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 905(1) the directors' duty to draw up the draft terms and adopt them` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 905(1) the directors draw up the draft terms and adopt them` AT 12

-- s 905(1): nothing done yet and no clock: the duty stays open however long the trace waits.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 905(1) the directors' duty to draw up the draft terms and adopt them` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 902(1)(a): the company is not a public company, so Part 27 does not apply and no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 905(1) the directors' duty to draw up the draft terms and adopt them` `scheme: not a public company` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 906(1) and s 906A(4), delivery to the registrar`

-- s 906(1): the directors deliver a copy of the draft terms on day 3; the text gives the directors no time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(1) the directors' duty to deliver the draft terms or the website notice to the registrar` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 906(1) the directors deliver a copy of the draft terms to the registrar` AT 3

-- s 906A(4): a company that relies on the website route delivers a notice giving details of the website on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(1) the directors' duty to deliver the draft terms or the website notice to the registrar` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 906A(4) the directors deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website` AT 3

-- s 902(3): the company is being wound up, so Part 27 does not apply and no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(1) the directors' duty to deliver the draft terms or the website notice to the registrar` `scheme: company being wound up` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 906(3) and s 906A(5), the registrar publishes at least one month before the meeting`

-- s 906(3): the registrar publishes on day 10, well before the last day (2 March 2026 is day 29).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `the receipt date` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906(2) the registrar publishes in the Gazette notice of receipt of the draft terms` AT 10

-- s 906(3): the registrar publishes on day 29, 2 March 2026, exactly one month before the meeting on 2 April 2026: "at least one month before".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `the receipt date` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906(2) the registrar publishes in the Gazette notice of receipt of the draft terms` AT 29

-- s 906(3): the registrar publishes on day 30, 3 March 2026, less than one month before the meeting.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `the receipt date` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906(2) the registrar publishes in the Gazette notice of receipt of the draft terms` AT 30

-- s 906(3): the copy reaches the registrar on 10 March 2026, after the last day for the notice (2 March 2026).
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `a receipt date too late for the notice` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1)

-- s 906(3): the copy reaches the registrar on 2 March 2026, the last day for the notice, so the registrar must publish that same day (day 0), and does.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `a receipt date on the last day for the notice` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906(2) the registrar publishes in the Gazette notice of receipt of the draft terms` AT 0

-- s 906A(5): a company that relies on its website: the registrar publishes the notice giving details of the website on day 29.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE `the receipt date` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906A(5) the registrar publishes in the Gazette the notice giving details of the website` AT 29

-- s 902(1)(a): not a public company, so no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(3) the registrar's duty to publish the notice at least one month before the meeting` `scheme: not a public company` FALSE `the receipt date` `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 906(2) with no meeting summoned: the registrar publishes on day 100; the text gives no time and no date for a month to run from.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(2) the registrar's duty to publish the notice where no meeting is summoned` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the registrar` DOES `s 906(2) the registrar publishes in the Gazette notice of receipt of the draft terms` AT 100

-- s 906(2) with no meeting summoned: nothing published yet and no clock: the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 906(2) the registrar's duty to publish the notice where no meeting is summoned` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 902(3): the company is being wound up, so no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906(2) the registrar's duty to publish the notice where no meeting is summoned` `scheme: company being wound up` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§§ `Traces: s 906A(6), the draft terms stay on the website`

-- s 906A(6): day 0 is 2 March 2026, one month before the meeting; the terms are on the website from day 0 and are never taken down.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906A(6) the company's duty to keep the draft terms on its website throughout the period` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the draft terms are on the company's website when the period begins` AT 0
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 906A(6): the terms come off the website on day 31, 2 April 2026, the date of the meeting: the period ends "on" that date, so the last day is in the period.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 906A(6) the company's duty to keep the draft terms on its website throughout the period` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the draft terms are on the company's website when the period begins` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the company takes the draft terms off its website` AT 31

-- s 906A(6): the terms come off the website on day 32, 3 April 2026, after the meeting: the period has ended.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906A(6) the company's duty to keep the draft terms on its website throughout the period` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the draft terms are on the company's website when the period begins` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the company takes the draft terms off its website` AT 32

-- s 906A(6): the terms are put on the website only on day 1, so they were not there throughout the period that began on day 0.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 906A(6) the company's duty to keep the draft terms on its website throughout the period` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 906A(6) the draft terms are on the company's website when the period begins` AT 1

-- s 906A(1): the company does not rely on the website route, so section 906A(6) puts no duty on it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 906A(6) the company's duty to keep the draft terms on its website throughout the period` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE `the meeting date` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

§§ `Traces: s 907, approval by the members at the meeting`

-- s 907(1): the meeting is held and the vote taken; three of four members in number and 80% in value: a majority in number representing 75% in value.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `classes: one class that votes for` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 907(1) the meeting of the members is held and the vote on the scheme is taken` AT 0

-- s 907(1): two of four in number is half, not a majority in number.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `classes: one class with exactly half in number` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 907(1) the meeting of the members is held and the vote on the scheme is taken` AT 0

-- s 907(1): exactly 75% in value is "representing 75% in value".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `classes: one class with exactly 75% in value` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 907(1) the meeting of the members is held and the vote on the scheme is taken` AT 0

-- s 907(1): 74% in value is short of 75%.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `classes: one class with 74% in value` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 907(1) the meeting of the members is held and the vote on the scheme is taken` AT 0

-- s 907(1): the meeting has not yet been held and the text gives no time: the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `classes: one class that votes for` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 907(2), s 917(2): all the securities of the transferor are held by the transferee and no meeting is required, so no duty to hold one arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 907(1) the company's duty to have the scheme approved at a meeting of its members` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, no meeting required` `classes: one class that votes for` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 908, the directors' explanatory report`

-- s 908(1): the directors draw up and adopt the report on day 20; the text gives no time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 908(1) the directors' duty to draw up and adopt the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 908(1) the directors draw up and adopt the explanatory report` AT 20

-- s 908(1): no report yet and no clock: the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 908(1) the directors' duty to draw up and adopt the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 915(4): all the relevant securities are held by the transferee, so the requirements of section 908 do not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 908(1) the directors' duty to draw up and adopt the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 915A(2): 92% held but the second condition (fair and reasonable consideration) is not met, so section 908 still applies.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 908(1) the directors' duty to draw up and adopt the explanatory report` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, second condition not met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 909, the expert's report`

-- s 909(1), (3): no joint expert is approved, so a separate expert's report is drawn up on behalf of the company, on day 20.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 909(1) the company's duty to have an expert's report drawn up` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 909(1) a separate expert's report is drawn up by a separate expert on behalf of the company` AT 20

-- s 909(3): the court has approved a joint expert, so a single report is drawn up on behalf of all the merging companies.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 909(1) the company's duty to have an expert's report drawn up` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 a merging company` DOES `s 909(1) a single expert's report is drawn up by the joint expert on behalf of all the merging companies` AT 20

-- s 909(7), s 918A(1): the reports are dispensed with by agreement, so section 909 does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 909(1) the company's duty to have an expert's report drawn up` `scheme: absorption, reports dispensed with by agreement` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 909(3): all the merging companies have applied jointly and the court approves on day 5; the text gives the court no time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 909(3) the court's power to approve the appointment of a joint expert` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the court` DOES `s 909(3) the court approves the appointment of a joint expert` AT 5

-- s 909(3): the joint application is made and the court has not acted: the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 909(3) the court's power to approve the appointment of a joint expert` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 909(3): no joint application, so the court has no power to approve a joint expert and nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 909(3) the court's power to approve the appointment of a joint expert` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 910, the supplementary accounting statement and its date limit`

-- The last annual accounts relate to a financial year ending on 1 September 2025, before 2 September 2025, the date seven months before the meeting on 2 April 2026: s 910(1)(a)
-- applies. The draft terms were adopted on 20 February 2026; three months before is 20 November 2025.
-- s 910(2)(a): the balance sheet is as at 20 November 2025, exactly three months before the adoption: "not more than three months before".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` (Date 1 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 910(1A) the directors prepare a supplementary accounting statement` AT 5

-- s 910(2)(a): the balance sheet is as at 19 November 2025, more than three months before the adoption.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` (Date 1 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 19 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 902-918 the directors of a merging company` DOES `s 910(1A) the directors prepare a supplementary accounting statement` AT 5

-- s 910(1)(a): the financial year ended on 2 September 2025, which is not before the date seven months before the meeting (2 September 2025), so the section does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` (Date 2 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 910(1A): the company has made public a half-yearly financial report for a later period, so no statement is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` (Date 1 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) TRUE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 910(1A): the section applies, no half-yearly report, and the statement is not yet prepared; the text gives no time, so the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` (Date 1 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 915A(2)(c): 92% held with both conditions met, so section 910 does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, 92% held, both conditions met` (Date 1 9 2025) (JUST `the meeting date`) (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 910(1)(b): no meeting is required, so the six months run back from the adoption on 20 February 2026 to 20 August 2025; accounts for the year ended 19 August 2025 are earlier,
-- so the section applies and the statement is owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 910(1A) the directors' duty to prepare a supplementary accounting statement` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, no meeting required` (Date 19 8 2025) NOTHING (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (Date 20 11 2025) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 911, inspection of the documents`

-- s 911(1), (2): day 0 is 2 March 2026; the documents are open from day 0 and stay open past the meeting on day 31.
